{"type":"after","callId":"call@225","endTime":54117.222,"result":{"value":{"s":"\n    Home/Manual/Developer reference/Getting started with brx-mcp\n    \n\nGetting started with \nFrom  to a live game in six commands — plus the MCP tools for driving a gun from an AI agent\nLast verified 2026-08-27View as Markdown\nWhat the badges mean✅bench Verified on our bench📖official Official Battle Company docs🔍app Decoded from the Callsign app👥community Community-reported🧪software Built + software-tested📐spec Specified only🚧under construction Under constructionNothing unconfirmed is published — see Credits & sourcing.\n\n is the project's lab instrument: a pure-Python ( + ) CLI and MCP server that runs on whichever machine owns the Bluetooth radio — Windows, macOS or Linux. It enforces the known-safe list, refuses malformed frames, records every session, and has a  tool.Source: README.md (quickstart, Safety)\n\nSource: README.md\n\nSource: README.md; mcp/brx_mcp/__main__.py\n\nSource: README.md (Platform notes)\nCLI commands\n\n\nCommand\nWhat it does\n\n\n\n ·  ·  · \nDiscover, check, watch, probe a single gun\n\n\n ·  ·  · \nEarlier single-purpose game drivers (the §7e sequence)\n\n\n\nHosted match with live scoring; modes tdm ffa infection lms cs domination koth ctf extraction\n\n\n · \nHardware-free narrated simulations\n\n\n ·  ·  · \nDiagnostics, fleet battery/reachability sweep\n\n\n ·  ·  ·  · \nUSB device record, armory enrolment, persistent , reset\n\n\n ·  · \nDrive the ESP32 IR transceiver rig\n\n\nSource: mcp/brx_mcp/__main__.py (dispatch table)\nMCP tools (what an agent can call)\n\n\nTool\nPurpose\n\n\n\n ·  ·  · \nDiscovery and health\n\n\n ·  · \nSession management\n\n\n · \nWrite frames; anything outside the known-safe list needs \n\n\n · \nRead the buffered event stream / block on a message\n\n\n · \nRecord and diff sessions\n\n\n\n then \n\n\n\nParse a USB  record\n\n\nResources: , , \nThe protocol reference, the device registry, capture files\n\n\nSource: mcp/brx_mcp/server.py\nPlatform notes.macOS: grant your terminal Bluetooth permission; CoreBluetooth reports per-machine UUIDs instead of MAC addresses, so never pattern-match on address format and expect to re-scan per machine. Gen1 taggers use Bluetooth Classic —  is BLE-only, so pair in the OS and use the serial port (guide todo). Captures and the device registry live in .Source: README.md; CLAUDE.md; docs/gotchas.md\nRecommended first session (safe order)\n → note the address.  → confirm  and read the  reply.\n read-only: pull the trigger, get tagged by another gun, watch // — send no config yet.\n on two guns; confirm each echoes  on spawn.\nIf anything looks wrong: , then power-cycle — that always restores the tagger.\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §8; README.md\n\n\n  "}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@225"}
